ot getting the latest update  pushed to your tv  do check out the link in the description  below for a manual update based on some  reports it will appear that individuals  have reported that samsung is not  pushing the update automatically and  you'll need to have to do it yourself  the changes here mainly affect the  filmmaker mode preset which has been  pushing brightness levels higher than it  should be  the best way to really test this out is  to put on content you like and play  around with these settings to see which  preset suits your taste to ensure it's  not washed out  after all it's your tv and getting the  color preset that suits your taste is  the most important  unlike other reviews where i do have it  in my study the massive samsung s95b is  sitting in my living room there's a big  window to the left of the tv and we'll  see how it fares under this lighting  condition  another thing to note is that we'll be  testing this tv right out of the box  without any additional toggles to really  see how well samsung has set up the  average user for success  specs wise this tv can hit 1400 nits  sustain on hdr on paper  in all honesty users won't care how  bright a white pixel can go because  that's just like staring into a  floodlight the real game changer here is  how good colors on the screen look  overall this tv shines bright and really  sets it apart from the competition  because the qd oled doesn't use a white  sub pixel like other oled tvs it can  achieve higher color brightness the  results the same level of consistency  that i had experienced with the  alienware monitor  it's definitely a screen that anyone  will stop and do a double take while  this might be a little controversial i  like how samsung's intelligent picture  mode brings out the best with whatever  content you have on screen on the other  hand if you're looking to gain final  calibration on the s95b be sure to turn  this feature off in order to access the  full suite of color profiles  overall i found that filmmaker mode is  rather muted for my liking on default  and will definitely benefit from some  tweaks under the settings menu  something that we have noticed when it  comes to content that is extremely dark  oled tvs tend to struggle a bit  depending on the room lighting situation  in our test to get a good sense of  declare on the tv we found the screen to  be glossy overall  however once content hits the screen  it's hard to observe any reflections  unless you are picking them out  contrast wise it's difficult to find any  fault with this tv at all the  consistency of the panel has held up  well and has everything we have come to  love about olets in general  when it comes to viewing the tv from  differing angles the tv looks great from  pretty much every corner of the room  however if you are using this tv during  the day under bright lighting conditions  the glare and reflections can become  apparent when it comes to design the  samsung s95 qd oled tv is pretty much  what every consumer should demand from a  top tier tv slim with small bezels  you'll be getting more screen on the  3840 by 2160 display  one of the more important aspects to  note here is that we have four hdmi 2.1  ports that point towards the right and  downwards as you are facing the tv and  that leads us nicely to the best part  about using this tv which is for gaming  equipped with alrm and vrr samsung knows  all the features that ps5 and xbox  series x console owners want to gun for  plus this tv even has free sync support  which means it could be very well be  used as a monitor but this is way too  big to be used on a desk  samsung has a dedicated gaming dashboard  that allows you to toggle the preferred  picture profile to fit the genre of the  game you are playing i suspect that most  folks will leave it at a single setting  but at least there are some options on  offer while you might be too big for a  test there's nothing stopping you from  plugging in a pc and enjoying the tv not  only in 16x9 but you have the 21x9 or  32x9 option this is specifically for  folks who love playing games for the  ultra wide experience however do note  that because the screen is not curved  you'll be missing out on some level of  immersion as well at this point i'll say  samsung put in this fixture because they  simply could you're able to double check  if you're hitting the numbers and  ensuring that neither tv or console is  lacking off  overall one should expect to achieve  120hz refresh rate easily with a  response time of 5 milliseconds one of  the more challenging aspects once you've  gotten this tv is figuring out all these  settings while samsung's tizen os and ui  feel snappy out of the box it does take  some time for you to figure out where  all these menus lead to for the most  part all your major streaming services  can be found here so there's little  worry that you might not be able to find  the app they are looking for when it  comes to audio it's amazing how such gen  tvs are able to eke out so much quality  in a small frame i would say the balance  is solid overall  and if you like there's even an  equalizer to give users some control and  achieve their preferred audio settings  to really get the best out of the tv  it's recommended to pair this along with  a samsung samba over here we have the  q-990b soundbar  which allows one to unlock samsung's q  symphony function and make full use of  all available speakers from both tv and  samba remote controls don't get much  praise but the one included with the tv  does away with all the buttons  it's so simple and sleek now and it  charges via solar or usbc we clearly see  the shift of the streaming walls here  with this remote and it looks like the  only missing streaming service here is  hbo so if you made it to the end of this  video i'm not quite sure if you needed  more convincing the only tricky thing  now is whether the samsung s95 qd oled  tv is even readily available in your  market hence if you are looking for a tv  right now and would like to dip your  feet into some future tech this tv is  the one for you  it's surprising that the first gen qd  oled tv displays have been able to  perform so well right out of the box  plus it's been a consistent and  excellent experience that i first  witnessed with the alienware monitor if  you have any further questions i'm happy  to answer them in the comment section  below until the next tv review this is  gerald signing off  [Music]  you

